    {
      "date": "2026-07-21",
      "description": "National Average Gas Price Crosses $4 Mark",
      "details": "The national average for regular gasoline officially crossed the $4.00 per gallon mark, reaching $4.019, a substantial jump of 16 cents in one week. This increase, driven by rising crude oil prices and geopolitical tensions, signals increased financial pressure on consumers. Higher gas prices typically reduce disposable income, leading to decreased discretionary spending and potentially lower ROAS for DTC brands.",
      "intensity": 3,
